WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.108
A nuclear power station boils water to

2
00:00:02.108 --> 00:00:03.245
spin a turbine,

3
00:00:03.245 --> 00:00:04.894
just like a coal one.

4
00:00:04.894 --> 00:00:06.959
Only the source of heat is different.

5
00:00:07.359 --> 00:00:08.148
Inside the core,

6
00:00:08.148 --> 00:00:09.809
a neutron strikes a uranium atom and

7
00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:11.005
splits it.

8
00:00:11.005 --> 00:00:13.512
That releases heat and more neutrons,

9
00:00:13.512 --> 00:00:15.405
which split more atoms.

10
00:00:15.405 --> 00:00:17.086
This is a chain reaction.

11
00:00:17.486 --> 00:00:18.833
The fuel is uranium,

12
00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:21.050
packed into small ceramic pellets,

13
00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:23.105
stacked in long metal rods and bundled

14
00:00:23.105 --> 00:00:24.566
together in the core.

15
00:00:24.966 --> 00:00:27.439
Control rods soak up neutrons:

16
00:00:27.439 --> 00:00:29.401
push them in to slow the reaction,

17
00:00:29.401 --> 00:00:31.259
all the way in to stop it.

18
00:00:31.259 --> 00:00:33.697
A moderator slows neutrons so they keep

19
00:00:33.697 --> 00:00:35.111
splitting atoms.

20
00:00:35.511 --> 00:00:37.914
The heat turns water into steam.

21
00:00:37.914 --> 00:00:39.900
The steam spins a turbine,

22
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.431
the turbine drives a generator,

23
00:00:42.431 --> 00:00:43.905
and the steam is cooled back into

24
00:00:43.905 --> 00:00:44.820
water.

25
00:00:45.221 --> 00:00:46.788
Cooling towers like this one,

26
00:00:46.788 --> 00:00:47.915
or river and sea water,

27
00:00:47.915 --> 00:00:49.190
do that job.

28
00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:52.794
Most of India's reactors are pressurised heavy-water

29
00:00:52.794 --> 00:00:54.164
reactors.

30
00:00:54.164 --> 00:00:56.533
Heavy water is such a good moderator

31
00:00:56.533 --> 00:00:58.750
that they can run on natural uranium,

32
00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:00.525
without enriching it.

33
00:01:00.924 --> 00:01:02.108
For GS Three:

34
00:01:02.108 --> 00:01:03.536
fission, heat, steam,

35
00:01:03.536 --> 00:01:04.465
turbine.

36
00:01:04.465 --> 00:01:06.392
And heavy water is what lets India

37
00:01:06.392 --> 00:01:08.376
use natural uranium.

